**How to implement.** The constructor windows compose the real study-fit host, and the Inverse flow is proved end to end through a shown window and a real kit folder: it ends at the study view (the S11.5 brief 'The Inverse flow ends at the study view'; 001 §N 'Long fits run on `JobRunner`'; .spec-md §0.1 `Program.fs`; AGENTS.md: wait for deterministic conditions, drive by id). (1) `OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs`, `ConstructorScene.mount` (steps 189, 233, 312): the shell it builds gains `studyFits = StudyFitJobHost.onUiThread (fun p -> dispatch (StudyFit (StudyFitProgressed p))) (fun r -> dispatch (StudyFit (StudyFitEnded r)))` (steps 393, 412), over the dispatch the mount captures from its init command, so a fit runs on a thread-pool worker and its progress and end arrive on the window's own thread. The docs of `MainConstructorWindow` and `InverseConstructorWindow` say, in no more words, that the Inverse window's study runs its fits off the UI thread. No other seam changes. (2) `AGENTS.md`, after the gotcha 'Lab files are read through import profiles' (step 312), one bullet of at most six lines: **The Inverse flow ends at the study** (`Studies.fs`, `StudyEngine.fs`, `StudyPublishing.fs`, spec 0050 S11): the Inverse constructor's flow strip adds Unknowns → Fit → Results → Publish after Data (S14 inserts Plan before Fit); a study fits experiments of one kit; its fit runs on `JobRunner` through the shell's `StudyFitJobHost` and writes one append-only `<study>@<stamp>.fitrun-json` on completion; Publish calibration writes each item's next revision (`CalibratedParameter`), and Promote to library mints the entry's next library version under `FitProvenance` and snapshots it into the kit. There is no hand-off window. Nothing else in the file changes. (3) Tests. `KitWindowTests` gains, with trait `ui-smoke`, `acceptance: the Inverse constructor creates a study in its kit and runs its fit off the UI thread, telling why it ended`: a shown `InverseConstructorWindow` over `TestAppScope.freshAppContext (FolderName "KitWindowTests")` and a kit from `TestAppScope.openedKitIn` (step 152), driven by id at the controls' centres: pressing `flowUnknownsStep`, setting `newStudyNameField`'s text to `Empty` and pressing `createStudyButton`, then `flowFitStep` and `studyRunFitButton`, and waiting through `Dispatcher.UIThread.RunJobs` until `studyFitErrorText` shows text, within ten seconds and never by a sleep, leaves the kit's folder holding `Empty.study-json` and no `.fitrun-json`, and `studyFitErrorText` holding `the stage has no run to fit` (step 385's `NoStageRunErr` through `FitStageErr`, step 386): the fit ran through the real host on a worker and its end was posted back to the window. The windows' other consumers keep their assertions.

**Acceptance.** After the windows are wired, a constructor window's shell MUST hold `StudyFitJobHost.onUiThread` over the window's dispatch, a study created in a real Inverse window MUST be written to its kit and its fit MUST run off the UI thread and report its end in the Fit step, and AGENTS.md MUST carry the gotcha 'The Inverse flow ends at the study'; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `acceptance: the Inverse constructor creates a study in its kit and runs its fit off the UI thread, telling why it ended`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s40 invariants MUST pass.
